{
  "slug": "artist:dj-slugo",
  "name": "DJ Slugo",
  "editorial_article": "Thomas Kendricks, known professionally as DJ Slugo, has been a key producer in the Chicago ghetto house scene for over three decades. His 1995 release Like It Raw on Dance Mania established a raw, stripped-back aesthetic that defined the regional style, featuring tracks like 'Pajamas' and 'Eat It.' In 1996, he followed up with Where The Rats, further cementing his role as a foundational figure in the development of the genre. His production approach often centers on repetitive, hard-hitting drum programming and minimalist, repetitive vocal hooks intended for dance floor movement. Along with contemporaries like DJ Funk and DJ Deeon, Slugo helped build the Dance Mania label into an essential outlet for Chicago's underground house music.",
